# convertdepth

- Label: Convert Depth
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/convertdepth.html
- Summary (EN): The Convert Depth node converts depth layers between Depth, Distance and Height representations, so a depth layer can be used in another workflow or visualised as a heightfield. Listed as available since version 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Convert Depth convertit une couche de profondeur entre Depth, Distance et Height, et fixe la valeur attribuée aux rayons manqués.

- Inputs meaning: ["depth: the layer holding the incoming depth"]

- Key parameters: ["Source Space: Depth, Distance or Height, the incoming type", "Dest Space: Depth, Distance or Height; Height sets the output type info to height", "Zero Depth Value: value assigned to zero depths (missed rays), required when converting to Height"]

- Caveats: ["Zero values are treated as missed rays at infinite distance and need a Zero Depth Value when converting to Height", "Depth is perpendicular distance to the eye; Distance is Euclidean, so corners are farther than the centre in a Distance map", "The page does not give the exact conversion formulas"]

